      "id": "claim_affe71b14d5c410c8a19a23bcc9f5ca3",
      "statement": "You can use the @DataJpaTest annotation from the spring-boot-data-jpa-test module to test Data JPA applications. By default, it scans for @Entity classes and configures Spring Data JPA repositories. If an embedded database is available on the classpath, it configures one as well. SQL queries are logged by default by setting the spring.jpa.show-sql property to true. This can be disabled using the showSql attribute of the annotation.",
